e><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGAWA HIROYASU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ENDOH, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GETTO, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDE, ISAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, SHIGEHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, HIROYASU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A reinforcing material for wood which comprises a thermoplastic resin sheet (2) reinforced with carbon fibers and, laminated on at least one surface thereof, at least one phenol resin-impregnated sheet (1) being formed by impregnating a porous sheet with a phenol resin wherein a degree of curing is 70 % to 95 %. The employment of a phenol resin-impregnated sheet (1) having a thickness of 0.01 mm to 1.0 mm leads to the production of a reinforcing material for wood which is free of irregularity or curl and excellent in resistance to water, in strength and the like. The reinforcing material for wood is cured in one piece via the phenol resin-impregnated sheet (1) on the surface of wood to thereby reinforce a wood (veneer or laminated wood) material, which results in producing a reinforced wood. The reinforcing material for wood is excellent in adhesiveness with wood and easy to handle, and causes no environmental pollution since the use thereof does not cause the discharge of a waste such as releasing paper, while it exhibits a satisfactory effect on the reinforcement of wood.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce matériau de renfort pour bois est constitué d'une feuille de résine thermoplastique (2), elle-même renforcée par des fibres de carbone, et d'une feuille imprégnée de résine phénolique (1), apposée sur l'une de ses faces au moins, obtenue par imprégnation d'une feuille poreuse d'une résine phénolique, le degré de durcissement allant de 70 à 95 %. Le fait d'utiliser une feuille imprégnée de résine phénolique (1), d'une épaisseur comprise entre 0,01 et 1,0 mm, permet de produire un matériau de renfort pour bois, exempt d'irrégularités et sans tuilage, remarquablement résistant à l'eau, d'une excellente tenue mécanique et analogue. Ce matériau de renfort est mis à durcir d'une seule pièce, la feuille imprégnée de résine phénolique (1) se trouvant contre le bois (bois de placage ou bois stratifié) aux fins d'un meilleur renforcement. Ce matériau de renfort, qui adhère très bien au bois, est d'une manipulation aisée et non polluant dans la mesure où son utilisation n'entraîne pas de rejet de déchets tel que du papier détachable. Il renforce, de surcroît, fort bien le bois.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>